---
description: Common Lisp style for psac — naming, macros, types, tests, .asd handling
globs: ["**/*.lisp", "**/*.asd", "**/*.ros"]
---

# Common Lisp style

- 2-space indent; `lower-case-lisp-case` functions; `-p` predicates; `+constants+`;
  `*special-variables*`; `%private-constructors`.
- Docstrings on every exported function/macro; file-level `;;;;` banner comments explain
  the mechanism and its Lean counterpart where one exists.
- **Macros** only where they remove real duplication or encode the API (`adaptive-read`,
  `with-scenario`, `with-fresh-state` are the pattern); otherwise functions.
- **Types** where they clarify intent: struct slot `:type`s (note blame/label masks are
  `fixnum` — principal ids are capped accordingly), `check-type`/`assert` at API borders.
- **Conditions:** define specific condition types (`label-flow-error`,
  `height-invariant-error` style) with `:report`; use `cerror` when continuing is sane.
- **Tests:** Rove; new tests use `deftest-fresh` (isolated world per test); assert exact
  values (bills, charges, slices), not smoke checks.
- `.asd` files are Lisp source; keep `:components` order load-safe (`:serial t`) —
  specials must be defined in an earlier file than their first reference.
- Equality: pick the mod's `:test` deliberately (`eql` default; numbers compared across
  types need `=`; lists need `equal`).
